I merged the two invalid-profile checks into one condition and return the already-invalid `type` on the fallback path, avoiding a redundant branch and constant materialization.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if ( type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID )
        return type;

    if ( profile != NULL && profileIndex < profile->numFields )
        return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;

    return type;
}
```